Shopify Theme
├── Layout        → Main HTML structure
├── Templates     → Different page types
├── Sections      → Reusable page sections
├── Snippets      → Small reusable components
├── Assets        → CSS, JS, Images, Fonts
├── Config        → Theme settings
├── Locales       → Multi-language support

1. assets/
This folder contains everything related to styling and frontend functionality.

2. config/
This stores Theme Customizer settings.

3. layout/
This is the most important folder.
Contains:
    theme.liquid
    password.liquid
    theme.liquid

Think of it like:
    App.js or index.html of React.

Every page loads through:
    theme.liquid

It contains:
    {{ content_for_layout }}
Shopify replaces this with the current page.

4. locales/
Contains translations:
    en, fr, de, es, ja, etc.

Example:
Instead of writing:
    Add To Cart
you write:
    {{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}

Then Shopify automatically shows:
    English, French, German depending on language.

5. templates/
This tells Shopify
"What kind of page is this?"

Example:
    product.json
    collection.json
    page.json
    cart.json
    blog.json

Suppose customer opens:
    example.com/products/shoes

Shopify loads
    product.json
Inside
    product.json
you'll see something like:
    {
    "sections": {
        "main": {
        "type": "main-product"
        }
    }
    }

Meaning it loads:
    sections/main-product.liquid

Think of Templates like Page Router

6. sections/
This is where most development happens. Every page is built using Sections.

Example:
    Homepage
    Announcement
    Hero
    Collection
    Newsletter
    Footer
Each one is a separate file.

DYNAMIC SECTIONS
Every section has:
    {% schema %}

Example:
    {
        "name":"Hero",
        "settings":[
            {
                "type":"text",
                "id":"heading"
            }
        ]
    }

Merchant can edits Heading inside Theme Editor.

7. snippets/
Snippets are reusable components.

Suppose 
    Product Card 
is used in
    Homepage
    Collection Page
    Search Page
Instead of writing code 3 times,

create
    card-product.liquid
Then
    {% render 'card-product' %}